{
  "name": "Track who left your customers' companies and where they work now (champion tracking) with Apify and Google Sheets",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 760,
        "content": "## Track who left your customers and where they work now\n\n### Who's it for\nCustomer success and sales teams: a champion who leaves is a churn risk at the old account and a warm lead at the new one. This workflow lists both, by company domain.\n\n### How it works\n1. Reads the `domain` column of your Google Sheet (customer websites).\n2. **Former Employees Finder** (`b2bsearch/former-employees-finder`) returns people who left those companies after a given year, with their current title, current company and its domain.\n3. Appends one row per person to a results sheet, so you can filter by seniority and reach out at the new employer.\n\n### Setup steps\n- Add your Apify credential to the Apify node.\n- Pick the input sheet (column `domain`) and the output sheet.\n- Optional: change `leftAfterYear`, add `titleKeywords` or `seniority` in the Apify node body.\n\n### Requirements\n- Apify account. $0.10 per page of up to 50 people; `previewOnly: true` counts for free first.\n- Google Sheets credential.\n- For the email at the new company, pass `linkedinUrl` to the LinkedIn Email Finder template.\n\n### Disclosure\nThe Apify Actor in this template is built by the author of the template. It is pay per result: a miss is a free row."
      },
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -900,
        -220
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "width": 420,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "## 1. Customer domains\nOne per row. Brand domains resolve to the owner.",
        "color": 7
      },
      "name": "Note: read",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -380,
